d 'EXTVGC': module to perform Extreme time-varying Granger-Causality test (EX-TVGC)
d
d  extvgc implements the extreme time-varying Granger-causality
d test of Hong, Guo and Zhao (2025, Research in International
d Business and Finance 77, 102994). The shocks of both series are
d split with quantile thresholds into extreme positive, extreme
d negative and normal shocks (Wang, Ma, Niu and He 2020, Economic
d Modelling), cumulated, and tested pair by pair in a lag-augmented
d VAR with the forward, rolling or recursive evolving algorithm of
d Shi, Phillips and Hurn (2018, 2020). Critical values come from a
d residual bootstrap over a control window. The command reports the
d maximum statistics, bootstrap critical values and dated causality
d episodes, reproduces Tables 1-3 of the paper (descriptive
d statistics, multivariate normality/ARCH, lag order), and draws
d the shocks, the overall test and the panel of all pairs. Option
d threshold(zero) gives the Hatemi-J (2012) positive/negative split
d in the same framework. 
d
d KW: Granger causalitty
d KW: time series
d KW: time varying
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261126
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f extvgc.ado
f extvgc.sthlp
f extvgc_methods.sthlp
f extvgc_example.do
